---
import EntetePage from '~/components/EntetePage.astro';
import site from '~/data/site.json';
import { chemin } from '~/i18n/config';

const c = site.contact;
const verif = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'Europe/Madrid',
}).format(new Date(site.cookies.verifie_le));
---
<EntetePage
  surtitre="Your data"
  titre="Cookies"
  chapo="This site sets no cookies. None. This page explains what is actually stored on your device, and why there is no consent banner to accept."
  ariane={[{ libelle: 'Cookies' }]}
  registre="papier"
/>
<section class="section conteneur">
  <div class="prose">

    <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No cookie is set, neither ours nor anyone else’s.</li>
      <li>There is no audience measurement tool — no Google Analytics, no equivalent. We do not know how many people visit this site.</li>
      <li>There is no external script, no share button, no embedded video.</li>
      <li>The fonts are hosted on our own domain: your browser contacts no outside server to display a page.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Checked on {verif} by loading several pages of the site in a clean browser: no
      <code>Set-Cookie</code> header, no cookie recorded, no outgoing request to another domain.
    </p>

    <h2>The only thing stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      If you press the light/dark button at the top, or if you pick a language, that preference is
      saved in your browser’s local storage. Nothing else.
    </p>
    <table class="tableau-stockage">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Key</th><th>Content</th><th>Created when</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>musima-theme</code></td>
          <td>The word <code>light</code> or <code>dark</code></td>
          <td>Only if you press the theme button</td>
          <td>Until you clear the site’s data</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>musima-langue</code></td>
          <td>A language code: <code>es</code>, <code>fr</code>, <code>en</code> or <code>ca</code></td>
          <td>Only if you pick a language in the selector</td>
          <td>Until you clear the site’s data</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      These values never leave your device: they are not sent to any server, not even ours. They
      cannot identify you or follow you from one site to another.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Why there is no banner to accept.</strong> Article 22.2 of Spanish Law 34/2002
      (LSSI-CE) exempts from consent anything strictly necessary for a service the user has
      expressly asked for. Remembering a display setting or a language you have just chosen
      yourself falls under that exception, as the Spanish Data Protection Agency reads it in its
      guidance on the use of cookies. Asking your permission for that would make no sense: the
      saving only happens if you click.
    </p>

    <h2>How to delete it</h2>
    <p>
      Clear the site data for <code>musima.org</code> in your browser settings, or use a private
      browsing window. The site works exactly the same without those values: it then follows your
      system’s light or dark theme, and the language of the address you are visiting.
    </p>

    <h2>The newsletter</h2>
    <p>
      Newsletter sign-up goes through {site.infolettre.fournisseur}, our sending provider. The form
      passes your address straight to that provider: no cookie is set on {site.nom} in doing so.
      The confirmation and unsubscribe pages hosted by the provider, on the other hand, are covered
      by its own cookie policy.
    </p>

    <h2>The host’s logs</h2>
    <p>
      Like any site, this one goes through a host — Cloudflare — which technically records incoming
      connections in order to serve the pages and protect itself from attacks. Those are server
      logs, not cookies: nothing is written to your device. See the
      {' '}<a href={chemin('en', 'confidentialite')} class="lien">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>If this ever changes</h2>
    <p>
      The day we add a statistics tool, an embedded video or any other third-party service capable
      of setting a cookie, two things would happen <em>before</em> switching it on: a consent
      banner would be put in place allowing you to accept or refuse, and this page would be
      updated. As long as you can read the opening sentence, there is nothing to consent to.
    </p>

    <h2>A question</h2>
    <p>
      Write to <a href={`mailto:${c.email}`} class="lien">{c.email}</a>. If you spot a cookie on
      this site, tell us: it would be a bug, and we would fix it.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .tableau-stockage { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: var(--t-200); }
  .tableau-stockage :is(th, td) {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--e-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--trait);
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .tableau-stockage th {
    font-family: var(--f-titre);
    font-size: var(--t-100);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--encre-faible);
    border-bottom-color: var(--trait-fort);
  }
</style>
